summary:
  The writer's curl buffers its output.

history:
  A stop travels up the writer's pipe a block at a time: ffmpeg, cat and
  curl each learn of it with the next one. Measured on a 2 kB/s station, where
  curl took two seconds to fill 4 KiB: the three were gone 3, 5 and 7 s after
  the stop, and within 2 s with -N.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SlideLogic.js

find:
          + "curl -sS -N -L --http0.9 -K "

replace:
          + "curl -sS -L --http0.9 -K "

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_slidelogic.qml::test_the_writer_looks_before_it_cuts_and_never_names_the_address.
